WEBVTT

00:00:00.300 --> 00:00:04.850 line:6% position:50% align:center
The “Christ” in “Jesus Christ” —
is it Jesus’ last name?

00:00:04.900 --> 00:00:07.656 line:6% position:50% align:center
The name at the end
of every prayer.

00:00:07.800 --> 00:00:11.148 line:6% position:50% align:center
We have found the Messiah
(which means Christ).

00:00:14.100 --> 00:00:19.513 line:6% position:50% align:center
Christ is not a last name.
It means “the Anointed One” — the Messiah.

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:27.753 line:6% position:50% align:center
God set apart kings, priests, and prophets
by anointing them with oil.

00:00:28.900 --> 00:00:33.576 line:6% position:50% align:center
Then Samuel took the horn of oil
and anointed him in the midst of his brothers.

00:00:36.000 --> 00:00:39.283 line:6% position:50% align:center
And he poured some of the anointing oil on Aaron’s head

00:00:39.900 --> 00:00:42.884 line:6% position:50% align:center
you shall anoint to be prophet in your place.

00:00:44.300 --> 00:00:48.828 line:6% position:50% align:center
Many people waited for the Messiah
only as a king who would drive out Rome.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.905 line:6% position:50% align:center
One day, after Jesus had come,
Peter made a confession.

00:00:55.300 --> 00:00:57.093 line:6% position:50% align:center
You are the Christ,

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.019 line:6% position:50% align:center
From then on, Jesus said
he must suffer and be killed,
and on the third day rise again.

00:01:07.100 --> 00:01:09.477 line:6% position:50% align:center
Far be it from you, Lord!

00:01:11.400 --> 00:01:15.074 line:6% position:50% align:center
To Peter, a Christ who dies
made no sense.

00:01:16.000 --> 00:01:18.558 line:6% position:50% align:center
But that road
had already been written.

00:01:20.700 --> 00:01:25.903 line:6% position:50% align:center
But he was pierced for our transgressions;
he was crushed for our iniquities;

00:01:27.600 --> 00:01:30.659 line:6% position:50% align:center
On the cross,
the cry of Jesus.

00:01:31.500 --> 00:01:35.918 line:6% position:50% align:center
My God, my God, why have you forsaken me?

00:01:37.700 --> 00:01:43.850 line:6% position:50% align:center
This cry is the first line of a psalm
written a thousand years before
by David, the anointed king.

00:01:43.900 --> 00:01:48.073 line:6% position:50% align:center
My God, my God,
why have you forsaken me?

00:01:49.600 --> 00:01:54.150 line:6% position:50% align:center
they divide my garments among them,
and for my clothing they cast lots.

00:01:54.200 --> 00:01:59.249 line:6% position:50% align:center
Beneath the cross, the soldiers
divided his garments and cast lots for his tunic.

00:01:59.300 --> 00:02:04.980 line:6% position:50% align:center
Peter, who once said “Far be it from you,”
after meeting the risen Jesus, preached this:

00:02:05.030 --> 00:02:11.559 line:6% position:50% align:center
God anointed Jesus of Nazareth with the Holy Spirit and with power. He went about doing good

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:17.915 line:6% position:50% align:center
They put him to death by hanging him on a tree,

00:02:19.500 --> 00:02:22.113 line:6% position:50% align:center
but God raised him on the third day

00:02:23.100 --> 00:02:28.288 line:6% position:50% align:center
A suffering Christ was not a failure —
it was the road the Scriptures pointed to.

00:02:28.400 --> 00:02:29.369 line:6% position:50% align:center
King,

00:02:30.800 --> 00:02:31.857 line:6% position:50% align:center
Priest,

00:02:33.200 --> 00:02:34.256 line:6% position:50% align:center
Prophet,

00:02:35.800 --> 00:02:38.480 line:6% position:50% align:center
Three offices,
in one Person.

00:02:39.600 --> 00:02:45.450 line:6% position:50% align:center
“Christ” is not a last name.
It is the confession
that Jesus is that very Messiah.

00:02:45.500 --> 00:02:49.810 line:6% position:50% align:center
everyone who believes in him receives forgiveness of sins through his name.

00:02:51.000 --> 00:02:54.753 line:6% position:50% align:center
You are the Christ, the Son of the living God.
